review:
After a long and tiring day in Karol bagh, this place was the easiest place to check in. Located in the centre of market, this place has both standing and sitting arrangements. Options to eat start from chat papdi to veg thali. (No nonveg served here, although the name relates to Punjab 😉)

Ordered starters and main course.

@paneer_tikka
Paneer tikka was good in taste. Presentation was simple, nothing fancy. Preparation was quick and paneer pieces were soft and little crispy on top.

@pao_bhaji
Pao bhaji was less thick than expected and missed the spice. The buns were good however.

@palak_patte_ki_chaat
The name was different, but the presentation and taste was same as that of a...read more

Ek dum bakwaaaaaaaaaaaass

Absolutely unhygienic. The waiters are unhygienic. Seats are just too dirty. Jo order kiya tha, vaise ka vaisa chor diya. Uper se pay bhi kar k aaye hum.

@Cafe Punjab- I think you should shut down.

Superb dimsums, a focused menu which helps them deliver delicious product! Tried the Crystal Chicken, Prawn Har Gao, Sui Mai, the Spinach Roll & Chicken and Pepper Dumpling - each dimsum was perfect & that black bean sauce accompanying them is incredible. Thank god for a high street outlet offering amazing dimsums finally!

@Dimsum&Co
do not add more categories in the menu - the focus is your forté

I personally really loved the ambience, it gives off a very easy and comforting vibes. I ordered the pancakes and they were quite good! Though a little more variety on the menu would be greatly received.
Cheers!
@foodonsingh #foodoneats (insta) @coffeebond

Really amazing food. We ordered malai chaap, afghani momos for the starters and both of them were really good in taste.

@buttersinghthecurrysmuggler
@_tasty_table_delights

For the main course, we ordered dal makhani and paneer which was made with a unique style I guess, a little different from what we have normally but was really out of the world.

if you have donuty sweet tooth, then this place can satiate you! donuts are soft and yummy..can make you drool the moment you see them! my favs- dark knight-oreo lover ;)
chocolate decadence-i am a sinful chocoholic
double trouble and after knight..i am head over heels for chocolate,so i totally love this place. coffee is also good here but then nothing special about it. only that you can accompany coffee with donut. savoury options are also good if you dont want sweet things!

Fantastic butter chicken 🥰 and great service from MR. Tek Raj ji
@DLF phase 1 Gurgaon
