Entered this restaurant for a quick dinner after a review on another portal, and we were pleasantly surprised to see that Ansal Plaza is on a ride to revive its lost glory.
@Kofuku, is a quaint little restaurant in Ansal Plaza, a new establishment serving Japanese cuisine. We were surprised to see the seating arrangement, which looked like a traditional Japanese household - floor seating, similar to our Indian tradition, an extremely healthy way of eating if you ask me, but they also have the chair and table option for those who don't want to sit on the floor.
We started with the Tempura Asparagus roll, fresh sushi served beautifully, perfectly pickled ginger and strong was a bit and...read more

@kiarasoulkitchen offers a fine dining experience with a menu that is SOUL warming. Nothing is oily , fried or too greasy which in turn doesn’t mess up the natural aroma of the food, which is good !
We started with the pokchoy dumplings 🥟 Vietnamese paper rice roll , tempura sushi 🍣 and minestrone soup ( soup is a must try )The quinoa flower pot was so exquisite and colourful just like rose flower .
Mains were Nasi goreng with Soya satay - mild spicy and yum 😋 Bajra Upma infused with beet root ( so healthy ) Organic black rice with Thai green curry with paneer slices and BAO bhaji an innovative alteration to pao bhaji served with three varieties of bread ( my favourite was...read more

